## Managing System Updates and Security

System updates patch software vulnerabilities, fix bugs, and deliver system enhancements.

```
[ Security Advisories ] ➔ [ dnf check-update ] ➔ [ dnf update --security ] ➔ [ System Patched ]

```

### Update Operations

* `dnf check-update` scans configured repositories and lists all installed packages that have newer versions available.
* `dnf update` updates all installed software packages on the operating system to their latest versions.
* `dnf update --security` restricts software updates specifically to patches classified as security advisories, minimizing changes to production systems.

---

## Managing Software Repositories and Groups

Repositories supply software packages, while package groups allow installing related server roles with a single command.

```
[ Repository Configuration File: /etc/yum.repos.d/ ] ➔ [ dnf repolist ] ➔ [ Active Package Sources ]

```

### Repository and Group Utilities

* Configuration files for repositories are stored in the `/etc/yum.repos.d/` directory with the `.repo` extension.
* `dnf repolist` lists all currently active and enabled software repositories on the system.
* `dnf group list` displays pre-defined collections of software packages (e.g., "Development Tools" or "Web Server").
* `dnf groupinstall "Group Name"` installs all software components bundled within a specified package group.